# Lint rules

## Where lints come from

- Built-in lints ship in the mockspace engine: the quality lints and the five design-round lints (`changelist-required`, `changelist-doc-gate`, `changelist-lock`, `changelist-immutability`, `changelist-seal`), on at `error`.
- Pack lints come from the `[lint-crates]` packs in `mockspace.toml` (`no-std`, `no-alloc`, `no-dyn-dispatch`, `no-runtime-spawn`, `no-runtime-registration` and the rest). `cargo mock lints` lists every lint, its source and its severity here.
- Repo lints are `mock/lints/<name>.rs`, one lint a file, compiled into one library with the rest.
- `forbidden-imports` is configured, not written: `rules = [{ scope, forbidden, reason }]` under `[lints.forbidden-imports]`.

## The repo lints

| File | Refuses | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `engine_spawn_through_gate.rs` | an engine spawn that does not go through `spawn_one_pointer` | HARD_ERROR |
| `frozen_ledger.rs` | a frozen crate file its ledger does not hold | HARD_ERROR |
| `frozen_no_feature_gate.rs` | a `#![feature]` in a frozen crate | HARD_ERROR |
| `frozen_no_outside_source.rs` | a frozen file bringing in a file from outside the ledger | HARD_ERROR |
| `frozen_no_recursion_limit.rs` | a raised recursion limit in a frozen crate | HARD_ERROR |
| `no_process_words_in_comments.rs` | a comment naming a round, topic, changelist, megaround, audit or src/doc CL | ADVISORY |
| `vocabulary_discipline.rs` | a dead vocabulary term in source | ADVISORY |

## Writing one

- Export one of `pub fn lint() -> Box<dyn CrateLint>` (per crate), `cross_lint()` (every crate at once), `repo_lint()` (paths, no crates) or `message_lint()` (a commit message or forge body).
- Implement `Lint` (`name`, `description`, `default_severity`, and `per_file`, `markers_decide` where the defaults do not fit) and the kind's trait (`CrateLint::check` for a crate lint).
- A crate lint that walks `ctx.all_sources()` itself returns `false` from `per_file`; one that reads `ctx.source()` keeps the default and is run per file.
- Read the tree only through the context: `ctx.source()`, `ctx.all_sources()`, `ctx.tree()`, `ctx.registry()` and `ctx.view()`. Never `std::fs`, `std::process`, `std::env` or a walker; the run replays a lint by what it asked of the view.
- Return `LintError::with_severity(crate, line, name, message, severity)`, with `e.path` set to the crate-relative file.
- The message says what is wrong and what to write instead.
- Shared code and tests sit in a subdirectory, which discovery does not read, pulled in with `#[path = "<dir>/<file>.rs"] mod <name>;`. Copy `frozen/scan.rs` and `scan/code.rs`.
- Test every refused shape and every look-alike that passes, in `<lint>/tests.rs`. Run a lint through the runner with `mockspace::testkit` (`LintFixture`, `run`) where markers or severity matter.
- A new lint goes into `mockspace.toml` at its designed severity, and into the table above.

## Configuring

- `[lints.<name>]` takes `commit`, `build`, `push` (`off`, `info`, `warn`, `error`), `include` and `exclude` (crate-relative path globs), and `crates` and `exempt_crates` (crate-name globs, `{prefix}` for the crate prefix).
- `cargo mock --lint-only --commit`, `--lint-only` and `--lint-only --strict` run the commit, build and push gates.
- Never lower a gate or add an exempt crate to make work pass. A gate change is the maintainer's.

## A finding

- Fix the code. No `#[allow]`, `#[expect]` or `cfg_attr` around one.
- `// lint:allow(<name>) reason: <why>; tracked: #<id>` keeps one finding of that lint off its line or item, where the lint lets markers decide. `lint-allow-requires-task-id` wants the tracked id.
